## 7. Conditions attached

1. Monthly monitoring to include productive-rate by tenure band and by rail, reported to the
   model owner and to IMV.
2. Enhanced review volume to be reported monthly against the 2,600 capacity figure; breach of
   2,450 in any month triggers notification to IMV and FCRC.
3. IMV-03 to be addressed in R5.3 or a formal exception sought.
4. TM-R-118 to remain in force while IMV-02 is open; any proposal to retire it requires IMV
   agreement.

---

## 8. Conclusion

Release 5.2 performs materially better than Release 5.1 on the measures at §4.1 and §4.2 and is
supportable for production use subject to the conditions at §7. Two medium findings are accepted
with compensating controls; one medium finding is carried forward; one matter (IMV-04) is
unresolved between IMV and the model owner and has been escalated.

Residual risk is recorded against the Head of Financial Crime Analytics as model owner, with the
enhanced-review capacity element (IMV-04) recorded against the Head of Financial Crime Operations.
Both entries are reflected in the model inventory and in the FCRC action log.

